  "worked_solution": "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(x)\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x.$ \n\nDifferentiating the above with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{\u2032} & ={u}^{\u2032}\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x+3u\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x \\\\ {y}_{2}^{\u2033} & ={u}^{\u2033}\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x+6{u}^{\u2032}\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x-9u\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({u}^{\u2033}\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x+6{u}^{\u2032}\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x-9u\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x)+9u\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x & =0 \\\\ {u}^{\u2033}\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x+6{u}^{\u2032}\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x & =0 \\\\ {u}^{\u2033} & =-6{u}^{\u2032}\\operatorname{cot}\u20613x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{\u2032}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\n{w}^{\u2032}=-6w\\operatorname{cot}\u20613x.\n$$\n\nThis is a separable equation that has the solution\n\n$$\nw={c}_{1}{csc}^{2}\u20613x.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{\u2032},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{\u2032}={c}_{1}{csc}^{2}\u20613x\\,\u27f9\\,u=-\\frac{{c}_{1}}{3}\\operatorname{cot}\u20613x+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(x)=u\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x(-\\frac{{c}_{1}}{3}\\operatorname{cot}\u20613x+{c}_{2}).\n$$\n\nFinally, setting ${c}_{1}=-3$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}\u20613x(\\operatorname{cot}\u20613x)=\\operatorname{cos}\u20613x.\n$$",
